{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For the turning away</b> — from <b>בשובה ונחת</b> (in repose and tranquility). The sense is <b>and the composure of fools</b>, and its meaning: the complacency of the simple destroys them — it kills them, for when they have ease they do evil, and when they are at ease from worldly troubles, that complacency destroys them. Another interpretation, in the vein of <b>שלו כל בוגדי בגד</b> (all betrayers are at ease), like <b>אשר חוטא עושה רע</b> (one who sins does evil) and so on; therefore <b>מלא לב</b> (the heart is full) and so on — and this is the correct one."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:27.528004951Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}